Sir!

112
00:09:22,067 --> 00:09:25,067
Ride the current and retreat from the palace!

113
00:09:25,067 --> 00:09:26,067
Dammit!

114
00:09:26,067 --> 00:09:27,067
I didn't think they'd pull back!

115
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:29,067
Now what?

116
00:09:29,067 --> 00:09:32,107
Here, take one of these, boss. That'll fix you right up.

117
00:09:35,567 --> 00:09:37,947
Don't look back. We're almost there.

118
00:09:38,687 --> 00:09:40,887
Pass through the gate and head inland.

119
00:09:41,507 --> 00:09:44,227
We gotta move, old man. Pull it together.

120
00:09:45,827 --> 00:09:48,827
Truly, there is nothing so terrible as old age.

121
00:09:49,287 --> 00:09:52,487
My will is strong, but my body will not budge an inch.

122
00:09:52,907 --> 00:09:53,827
Not now!

123
00:09:57,487 --> 00:09:58,947
The king is injured.

124
00:09:59,067 --> 00:10:00,207
Your highness!

125
00:10:01,107 --> 00:10:03,047
Aw, crap. What should we do?

126
00:10:03,687 --> 00:10:06,807
Nothing. This is the end, I'm afraid.

127
00:10:06,987 --> 00:10:07,887
What? No!

128
00:10:13,967 --> 00:10:15,707
Ah! Hoey!

129
00:10:18,407 --> 00:10:19,707
We're saved!

130
00:10:22,227 --> 00:10:24,187
I owe you my life, Hoey.

131
00:10:25,087 --> 00:10:27,667
Don it all. I can't even turn my head.

132
00:10:27,667 --> 00:10:29,267
You're not that old.

133
00:10:29,387 --> 00:10:30,167
Well done, Hoey.

134
00:10:30,587 --> 00:10:31,987
Now come join us and hurry.

135
00:10:32,987 --> 00:10:33,427
Faster!

136
00:10:34,247 --> 00:10:35,547
I'm gonna pass out.

137
00:10:35,547 --> 00:10:50,507
What's wrong now?

138
00:10:50,507 --> 00:10:50,567
What's wrong now?

139
00:10:50,567 --> 00:10:54,867
Did we get snagged on something back there?

140
00:10:54,867 --> 00:11:09,887
Oh, no! Your highness!

141
00:11:09,887 --> 00:11:09,907
Oh, no! Your highness!

142
00:11:12,907 --> 00:11:14,027
Already grabbed him.

143
00:11:14,247 --> 00:11:15,327
He can't pull away.

144
00:11:15,687 --> 00:11:17,267
The pirates aren't fleeing either.

145
00:11:17,267 --> 00:11:19,607
I thought that swordsman took care of him already.

146
00:11:19,607 --> 00:11:21,727
Why the hell is he giving us so much trouble?

147
00:11:22,067 --> 00:11:23,667
Minister, let's go back.

148
00:11:23,927 --> 00:11:25,567
At this rate, the king could be killed.

149
00:11:26,787 --> 00:11:29,107
I told you to retreat, didn't I?

150
00:11:30,607 --> 00:11:32,707
All is not lost if you escape.

151
00:11:33,207 --> 00:11:35,807
Bring my son, and we may see victory yet.

152
00:11:35,807 --> 00:11:44,167
There's no time. Do as our lord commands!

153
00:11:44,667 --> 00:11:45,327
Yes, sir!

154
00:11:45,987 --> 00:11:47,507
Both are getting away!

155
00:11:47,787 --> 00:11:48,987
Should we go after them?

156
00:11:49,267 --> 00:11:50,127
Let him run.

157
00:11:50,367 --> 00:11:51,247
What do we care?

158
00:11:51,787 --> 00:11:55,347
Soldiers who can't protect their king are no threat to us.

159
00:11:56,187 --> 00:11:59,507
Speaking of the king, tie him up in case he gets his strength back.

160
00:12:00,007 --> 00:12:00,747
Yes, sir!

161
00:12:00,747 --> 00:12:03,147
I have failed you this time.

162
00:12:03,907 --> 00:12:06,867
But so long as my allies live, the battle is not over!

163
00:12:07,607 --> 00:12:07,927
Yeah!

164
00:12:09,667 --> 00:12:10,227
Yeah!

165
00:12:16,227 --> 00:12:16,747
What?

166
00:12:16,827 --> 00:12:17,587
What's that?

167
00:12:17,927 --> 00:12:18,547
Don't know.

168
00:12:18,987 --> 00:12:21,027
Maybe the water washed in an old corpse?

169
00:12:25,267 --> 00:12:26,387
Prince Fukuboshi!

170
00:12:26,827 --> 00:12:29,447
Have you any news regarding the missing Straw Hat Pirates?

171
00:12:29,947 --> 00:12:30,547
No, sir.

172
00:12:31,127 --> 00:12:32,287
Nothing of use, at least.

173
00:12:32,807 --> 00:12:36,067
The patrons of this clothing store saw Straw Hat and three others shopping.

174
00:12:36,447 --> 00:12:38,907
But they were apparently all taken away by King Neptune.

175
00:12:39,547 --> 00:12:43,327
Well, that would account for the members who seized the palace, but none other.

176
00:12:43,787 --> 00:12:44,247
Yes, sir.

177
00:12:44,907 --> 00:12:46,107
Then where could they be?

178
00:12:46,847 --> 00:12:50,427
What do we know about the two crew members who were seen in Coral Hill earlier today?

179
00:12:51,427 --> 00:12:54,647
We asked around, but no luck so far, Solop.

180
00:12:55,367 --> 00:12:58,707
Alas, this may prove more complicated than I had hoped.

181
00:12:59,567 --> 00:13:01,067
Shake it, shake it, shake it.

182
00:13:01,067 --> 00:13:02,087
It'll be fine, bro.

183
00:13:02,527 --> 00:13:06,147
Maybe we should call the palace again and see if there's something they're not telling us.

184
00:13:06,467 --> 00:13:08,187
Hey, maybe that's them now!

185
00:13:08,987 --> 00:13:09,787
Prince Fukuboshi!

186
00:13:10,207 --> 00:13:10,567
Sir!

187
00:13:10,987 --> 00:13:11,387
Come in!

188
00:13:11,507 --> 00:13:12,087
Uh-oh.

189
00:13:12,087 --> 00:13:14,407
Yes, this is Fukuboshi.

190
00:13:14,807 --> 00:13:17,327
There's an urgent situation over here in Waterwheel Town.

191
00:13:17,447 --> 00:13:18,627
We're requesting assistance.

192
00:13:18,747 --> 00:13:18,887
Hmm?

193
00:13:19,247 --> 00:13:20,087
Please explain.

194
00:13:20,887 --> 00:13:23,627
Men from the Fishman District suddenly invaded the town.

195
00:13:23,887 --> 00:13:25,707
They have some grudge against the Queen.

196
00:13:25,707 --> 00:13:31,527
Sorry, but this is invite only, pal.

197
00:13:36,747 --> 00:13:39,307
Wait, what do you mean they have a grudge against my mother?

198
00:13:39,567 --> 00:13:40,007
Tell me!

199
00:13:40,207 --> 00:13:40,787
Are you there?

200
00:13:42,227 --> 00:13:43,527
To Waterwheel Town!

201
00:13:43,847 --> 00:13:44,147
Quickly!

202
00:13:44,447 --> 00:13:45,147
Yes, sir!

203
00:13:49,787 --> 00:13:50,907
Are they gone?

204
00:13:51,287 --> 00:13:53,567
Yeah, to deal with the others, I guess.

205
00:13:53,567 --> 00:13:55,647
This is a mess.

206
00:13:56,087 --> 00:13:57,867
Dosun couldn't wait for the rest of us.

207
00:13:58,207 --> 00:14:01,967
I know he's eager to fight, but the whole point was to attack every place at once.

208
00:14:02,567 --> 00:14:03,047
Whatever.

209
00:14:03,727 --> 00:14:05,427
No point in complaining now.

210
00:14:06,567 --> 00:14:07,727
Listen up, men!

211
00:14:08,167 --> 00:14:10,787
This is the day that our dreams finally come true!

212
00:14:11,207 --> 00:14:14,047
Draw your swords and fight for a better tomorrow!

213
00:14:14,427 --> 00:14:14,907
Yeah!

214
00:14:14,907 --> 00:14:34,767
Oh!

215
00:14:34,767 --> 00:14:42,967
Ooh! So this is the sea forest, huh? I see why you wanted to come here.

216
00:14:42,967 --> 00:14:52,967
Thank you. I've wanted to see this place for so long. You have no idea how much this means.

217
00:14:57,467 --> 00:15:00,267
Hopefully we can get some peace and quiet here.

218
00:15:00,267 --> 00:15:05,267
Mermaids, whoo! Mermaids, whoo!

219
00:15:05,267 --> 00:15:07,267
Oh, man.

220
00:15:07,267 --> 00:15:09,267
Look, it's a Sunny!

221
00:15:09,267 --> 00:15:12,267
Hey, you're right! And I see Frankie, too!

222
00:15:12,267 --> 00:15:18,267
Hey, what's up? I didn't know you were here! Cool place, huh?

223
00:15:18,267 --> 00:15:21,267
Wow! Look who it is!

224
00:15:21,267 --> 00:15:27,267
Whoa, is that your new girlfriend? You always did like to aim big.

225
00:15:27,267 --> 00:15:36,267
Let me introduce you. This here is Crybaby!

226
00:15:36,267 --> 00:15:40,267
Doesn't look like a crybaby to me. Tell me, sister, do you live up to your name?

227
00:15:40,267 --> 00:15:45,267
Maybe a little bit. You may call me Shirohoshi if you please.

228
00:15:45,267 --> 00:15:48,267
So, uh, you're the only one here?

229
00:15:48,267 --> 00:15:54,267
I'm afraid so. Robin stopped by earlier, but she had some Robin business to attend to.

230
00:15:54,267 --> 00:15:58,267
She went to that big forest of coral over there. Who knows when she'll be back.

231
00:16:02,267 --> 00:16:03,267
Luffy!

232
00:16:03,267 --> 00:16:09,267
It's Jinbei! Awesome! You're here, too!

233
00:16:09,267 --> 00:16:12,267
I'm so pleased that you made it.

234
00:16:12,267 --> 00:16:28,267
You've grown even stronger than before. I can tell.

235
00:16:28,267 --> 00:16:32,267
People said you couldn't come to town, so I was afraid I wouldn't get to see you.

236
00:16:32,267 --> 00:16:35,267
I thought you came here because you received my message.

237
00:16:35,267 --> 00:16:39,267
Huh? What message? I didn't hear anything.

238
00:16:39,267 --> 00:16:41,267
Hmm. Most peculiar.

239
00:16:41,267 --> 00:16:44,267
A pleasure to see you, Jinbei. It's been ever so long.

240
00:16:44,267 --> 00:16:49,267
Yes. What an unexpected meeting, but a welcome one. To what do I owe thou-

241
00:16:49,267 --> 00:16:51,267
Whoa!

242
00:16:52,267 --> 00:16:55,267
What are you doing here? Shouldn't you be in the palace?

243
00:16:55,267 --> 00:17:00,267
Do you have a sec, Frankie? I need some help getting Sanji and Hachi off this shark.

244
00:17:00,267 --> 00:17:05,267
You got it! Whoa! It's the octopus guy!

245
00:17:05,267 --> 00:17:06,267
You...

246
00:17:06,267 --> 00:17:08,267
Looks like you took a beating, brother.

247
00:17:08,267 --> 00:17:09,267
Hachi!

248
00:17:09,267 --> 00:17:10,267
What?!

249
00:17:11,267 --> 00:17:12,267
You're injured!

250
00:17:12,267 --> 00:17:14,267
What happened? Scratch that!

251
00:17:14,267 --> 00:17:16,267
What are you doing on Fishman Island?

252
00:17:16,267 --> 00:17:20,267
I heard that Arlong was captured, so I assumed you were as well.

253
00:17:20,267 --> 00:17:24,267
You... long story... maybe later.

254
00:17:24,267 --> 00:17:27,267
Frankie! Let's get Sanji, too!

255
00:17:27,267 --> 00:17:29,267
That's alright. I'm feeling better.

256
00:17:29,267 --> 00:17:48,267
The mermaid princess at last. Standing here, I see how inadequate my imagination was!

257
00:17:48,267 --> 00:17:54,267
Even with all the colors in my heart, I could never paint a picture as lovely as you!

258
00:17:54,267 --> 00:17:56,267
Uh-huh.

259
00:17:56,267 --> 00:18:00,267
No blood loss. He's being annoying, but also sort of cool.

260
00:18:00,267 --> 00:18:02,267
The old Sanji is back!

261
00:18:02,267 --> 00:18:06,267
Alas! Such beauty as yours is too fast to fit on any canvas!

262
00:18:06,267 --> 00:18:07,267
It's a magical!

263
00:18:07,267 --> 00:18:09,267
